=== GRIND cycle 23, casting 1 -- the structural fix for the escalated class
=== closed-vocabulary-not-enforced-on-the-deciding-read (D-214, D-215).

# escalation.json has ONE writer and THREE readers. The resolver was PRIVATE
# to one of them, so the other two each grew their own opinion of one field:
# the report rendered ANY string verbatim and counted it in neither bucket
# (D-214), and the CLI dropped every non-mapping entry one line above its own
# unknown_status counter (D-215). The resolver is PUBLIC in schemas/vocab.py
# now and all three readers import it. One fixture, all three readers.

THE FIXTURE -- escalation.json classes:
    bogus-class      {"status": "BOGUS"}
    clean-class      {"status": "CLEARED", "exit_reason": "clean_cycles", "cleared_at_cycle": 2}
    live-class       {"status": "ESCALATED"}
    shapeless-class  "just a string"

== 1. Foundry-Gate(done) over the wire, server.call_tool -- ST-010 ==
    check                        escalated_classes_cleared (still escalated=3, latent_only=0)
    ok                           False
    classes                      ['bogus-class', 'live-class', 'shapeless-class']
    persisted_escalated_classes  ['bogus-class', 'live-class', 'shapeless-class']
    recurring_classes            []  <- every instance is fixed, so
                                    the PERSISTED read is what answered

== 2. Foundry-Report over the wire -- AC-004, the other terminal artifact ==
    Foundry-Report ok            True
    count                        4
    by_status                    {"CLEARED": 1, "ESCALATED": 3}
    sum(by_status.values())      4  <- D-214: was 2 while count was 3
    by_exit_reason               {"budget": 0, "clean_cycles": 1}
    row bogus-class      status=ESCALATED exit_reason=None
    row clean-class      status=CLEARED   exit_reason=clean_cycles
    row live-class       status=ESCALATED exit_reason=None
    row shapeless-class  status=ESCALATED exit_reason=None

== 3. scripts/measure-run.py over the SAME fixture -- FR-028 ==
    exit status                  0
    classes                      4
    by_status                    {"CLEARED": 1, "ESCALATED": 3}
    sum(by_status.values())      4  <- D-215: was 1 while classes was 4
    unknown_status               2  <- the entries the resolver DEFAULTED
    by_exit_reason               {"budget": 0, "clean_cycles": 1}

== 4. THE THREE READERS AGREE, which no per-reader pin can state ==
    gate still-escalated         ['bogus-class', 'live-class', 'shapeless-class']
    report non-CLEARED rows      ['bogus-class', 'live-class', 'shapeless-class']
    report/CLI by_status equal   True
    report count == its buckets  True
    CLI classes == its buckets   True

== 5. schemas/vocab.py#escalation_status -- total over the closed vocabulary ==
    ESCALATION_STATUSES          CLEARED ESCALATED
    {"status": "CLEARED"}  -> CLEARED   unknown=False
    {"status": "ESCALATED"} -> ESCALATED unknown=False
    {"status": "BOGUS"}    -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    {"status": "cleared"}  -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    {"status": "CLEARED "} -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    {"status": ""}         -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    {"status": null}       -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    {"status": 7}          -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    {}                     -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    "just a string"        -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    ["ESCALATED"]          -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    null                   -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    7                      -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    true                   -> ESCALATED unknown=True
    []                     -> ESCALATED unknown=True

